│  │ Dashboard │  │ MCP      │  │ CLI              │  │
│  │ (web)     │  │ Server   │  │ spec validate    │  │
│  └─────┬─────┘  └────┬─────┘  └────────┬─────────┘  │
│        │             │                │             │
│        └─────────────┼────────────────┘             │
│                      │                              │
│              ┌───────▼────────┐                     │
│              │  spec-api      │                     │
│              │  (REST)        │                     │
│              └───────┬────────┘                     │
│                      │                              │
│              ┌───────▼────────┐                     │
│              │  spec-engine   │                     │
│              │  (core logic)  │                     │
│              │                │                     │
│              │  parse → ontology → validate → sim  │
│              └───────┬────────┘                     │
│                      │                              │
│              ┌───────▼────────┐                     │
│              │  spec-db       │                     │
│              │  (SQLite/Postgres)                   │
│              └────────────────┘                     │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Stack

| Layer | Tech | Why |
|-------|------|-----|
| Core Engine | TypeScript | One language across API, MCP, codegen. Runs on Node/Bun/Deno. |
| API | Elysia (Bun) | Fast, TypeScript-native, OpenAPI auto-gen |
| MCP Server | @modelcontextprotocol/sdk | Standard protocol. Works with major AI coding agents. |
| Dashboard | React + Vite | Fast build, small bundle, no framework lock-in |
| Database | SQLite (embedded) → Postgres (cloud) | Start local, scale to cloud. Same schema. |
| CLI | Node.js + Commander.js | Zero-dependency install, single binary target |
| Codegen | AST transforms + templates | Reads spec ontology, outputs typed code |
| Sim Engine | TypeScript state machine | Pure functions. Spec → execution graph. |

## Constraints

- Monorepo. One `pnpm-workspace.yaml`. Shared types.
- SQLite for local/offline. Postgres for cloud. Same Prisma schema.
- MCP server must work with major AI coding agents — not just one.
- CLI must install via `npm install -g spec-platform` with zero additional deps.
- The platform IS dogfooded. `specs/` in this repo uses our own format.
- Free tier: 1 project, local-only, full features. Paid: teams, cloud, predictions.

## Success Criteria

1. [ ] `spec validate` runs on demo-project specs and produces a report
2. [ ] MCP server returns `getSpec("demo", "COPY.dog")` in under 50ms
3. [ ] CLI installs with `npm install -g` on macOS, Linux, Windows
4. [ ] Simulation runs a 6-step scenario and reports correct outcome
5. [ ] Dashboard shows project list with completeness scores
6. [ ] Codegen produces a working React component from DESIGN-SYSTEM.dog

---

## Branding

### Mascot

**Spec** — the spec dog. Lives on the website and in the CLI. Developers feed Spec by running `dotdog validate`. A fed Spec means clean specs.

### Visual

- SVG dog logo (amber, round face, floppy ears)
- Clean light theme on all surfaces
- Dog emoji 🐕 used sparingly in docs
- Hidden command: `dotdog woof` prints a small ASCII dog

### Interactive Widget

A virtual Spec lives on the website. Three interactions:

| Action | Dog | dotdog metaphor |
|--------|-----|-----------------|
| 🦴 Feed | Spec eats, gets happy | `dotdog validate` — specs are fresh |
| ✋ Pet | Spec wags tail | Morale boost |
| 🎾 Fetch | Spec retrieves | `dotdog compile` — fetch the .dag |

Hunger decays over time = specs go stale. Keyboard shortcuts: `V` (validate), `C` (compile), `P` (pet).

### Voice

- Tagline: "Feed the dog. Ship with specs."
- Tone: professional, friendly, subtle.
- "Dog fed" = validation passed. "Hungry dog" = specs are stale.
